    engine2d_vulkan_swapchain_registry_disconnect_2026-08-11, 1, "2026-11-13: On release/1.0.0 c8c3e7bc4f1, Linux aarch64 (DGX Spark GB10), Rust seed af717f53d6bce3e5 the source-level contract specs pass: engine_vulkan_present_api_spec 2/2, engine_vulkan_window_present_spec 7/7, engine2d_strict_vulkan_submit_no_readback_contract_spec 7/7. The old bridge symbols have no definition left. Blocked for closure on this host: the Acceptance section needs a live Xvfb or physical-display present with checksum, and this host has no Xvfb (xwd only) and the live tests are ignored Rust tests that go through Vulkan instance creation (other lane). Same missing evidence as engine2d_vulkan_window_8k_gate_is_device_present_proxy_2026-08-31."

bug_scope |bug_id, scope, root_layer, note|
    engine2d_vulkan_swapchain_registry_disconnect_2026-08-11, 4, "2026-11-12 lane triage (vulkan-mac lane, work/fix-vulkan-mac-20261112 @ 7a06b4aafd5). Source trace: engine.spl:3603 present_window_device -> backend_vulkan.spl:1989 _present_device (fail-closed without presentation_swapchain, present_readback_bytes=0, device-local copy) -> sffi_vulkan.spl:1349 vulkan_sffi_present_buffer{,_regions} -> rt_vulkan_present_buffer{,_regions} on the single rt_vulkan_init_window_present owner; compositor gates on both ends (vulkan_present_damage_gate.spl, host_compositor_core.spl receipt validation). The 2026-08-11 no-API disconnect is not present in this tree's source; only live presentation proof (Xvfb/physical display, zero-readback timed frames, 8K p50/p95) remains, needing a display environment + admitted compiler. No source change; stays open."

